lan. so this includes again a few different projects which you will see detailed out more in March but this approximately 1.9 million some of the funding will go towards the vision zero work approximately 2.7 million of the bond will be used to fund continuing work on our vision zero plan about 5.9 million will go towards various right-of-way improvements this includes continued work on South Duke Street, streetscapes on Anna Giudiana, and numerous signal upgrades throughout the city. About $1.6 million would go for some ongoing maintenance to our facilities, including roof repairs for some various buildings. It will also include some upgrades to the Welcome Center that are starting now and some other general maintenance needs. And finally, we've designated about $3.4 million toward expanding efficiencies for our operations center. We need to build a new salt shed, among other things. We have concerns that the current one won't be able to withstand the weather for much longer. And it also includes costs for upgrading storage, both for equipment and for our archives. So moving on, I'm going to actually jump to water next. There's about $17.6 million of the bond that will be designated for water. This consists of four main areas. The first and biggest is the water transmission Maine which we have discussed a few different times approximately ten and a half million will be designated for this work this is the main transmission line from the Susquehanna River the line is currently past its useful life and requires us to replace it to ensure that the water continues to flow at the capacity that we need to serve to serve all residents next is just some general water quality improvements. This category is about $3.6 million and includes a few different projects that are focused on maintaining or improving water quality. And again, those will be outlined in more detail in March. Another category is the lead service lines, replacement of those. We've discussed this numerous 